// User input-token-length vs. team peers — z-score outlier detection.
// No new columns/tables needed — pure measures over existing fields.
//
// STATISTICAL NOTE: compares each user's AVERAGE prompt length against
// the distribution of AVERAGE prompt lengths across their peers on the
// same team (customDimension1) — a two-level comparison (peer-of-peers),
// not a comparison against the pooled distribution of every individual
// request. That distinction matters: comparing against raw pooled
// requests would be dominated by whichever teammate sends the most
// requests and conflate "this user's typical prompt" with "how many
// requests everyone sent" — comparing averages-of-averages is the
// statistically correct way to ask "is this person's typical prompt
// length unusual for their team."
//
// SAME CAVEAT AS FILE 12: an atypical prompt length isn't inherently
// "wrong" — could reflect a genuinely different, valid task mix (someone
// doing long-document analysis on a team that mostly does short Q&A).
// Use this to prompt a conversation, not as a scorecard — see the
// visibility note in 12-prompt-chain-efficiency-measures.dax, the same
// guidance applies here.

// ============================================================
// THIS USER
// ============================================================

User Avg Input Tokens = AVERAGE('llm-usage-container'[promptTokens])

// ============================================================
// PEER BASELINE (all users sharing this user's cost center)
// ============================================================

// NOTE: a DAX measure always returns a scalar, never a table — so unlike
// the rest of this kit there's no way to factor "every appId on this
// user's team" out into its own reusable measure the way [Total Cost] is
// reused elsewhere. The CALCULATETABLE(...) below is repeated verbatim in
// both measures that need it; that's necessary duplication, not an
// oversight, given the syntax constraint.

Team Avg of User Averages =
AVERAGEX(
    CALCULATETABLE(
        VALUES('llm-usage-container'[appId]),
        ALLEXCEPT('llm-usage-container', 'llm-usage-container'[customDimension1])
    ),
    CALCULATE(AVERAGE('llm-usage-container'[promptTokens]))
)

Team StdDev of User Averages =
STDEVX.P(
    CALCULATETABLE(
        VALUES('llm-usage-container'[appId]),
        ALLEXCEPT('llm-usage-container', 'llm-usage-container'[customDimension1])
    ),
    CALCULATE(AVERAGE('llm-usage-container'[promptTokens]))
)

// ============================================================
// COMPARISON
// ============================================================

User Prompt Length Z-Score =
DIVIDE(
    [User Avg Input Tokens] - [Team Avg of User Averages],
    [Team StdDev of User Averages]
)

Has Sufficient Data for Comparison =
// Minimum-sample guard — a z-score from 2 requests or a 2-person "team"
// is noise, not a signal. Hide/gray out the outlier flag below this
// threshold rather than showing a confident-looking number built on
// nothing.
[Total Requests] >= 20
    && CALCULATE(DISTINCTCOUNT('llm-usage-container'[appId]), ALLEXCEPT('llm-usage-container', 'llm-usage-container'[customDimension1])) >= 3

Is Outside Typical Prompt-Length Band =
IF(
    NOT [Has Sufficient Data for Comparison], "Insufficient data",
    IF(ABS([User Prompt Length Z-Score]) > 2, "Outside typical range", "Typical")
)
